#### 2. LLM Service (REST API Wrapper)
This class handles LLM interactions using LangChain4j and a REST API (e.g., OpenAI).

```java
import dev.langchain4j.model.chat.ChatLanguageModel;
import dev.langchain4j.model.openai.OpenAiChatModel;

public class LlmService {
    private final ChatLanguageModel llm;

    public LlmService(String apiKey) {
        // Configure OpenAI as an example; replace with your preferred LLM
        this.llm = OpenAiChatModel.builder()
                .apiKey(apiKey)
                .modelName("gpt-3.5-turbo")
                .build();
    }

    public String generateResponse(String prompt) {
        try {
            return llm.generate(prompt);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println("LLM error: " + e.getMessage());
            return "Sorry, I couldn’t process that.";
        }
    }
}
```

#### 3. Issue-Specific Agents
Each agent uses the LLM to troubleshoot its specific issue.

```java
abstract class IssueAgent implements Agent<String> {
    protected final LlmService llmService;
    protected boolean active = true;

    public IssueAgent(LlmService llmService) {
        this.llmService = llmService;
    }

    @Override
    public String perceiveEnvironment() {
        return ""; // Input comes from Orchestrator, not direct user input
    }

    @Override
    public boolean handleError(Exception error) {
        communicate("Error: " + error.getMessage());
        return false;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean isActive() {
        return active;
    }
}

class CallAgent extends IssueAgent {
    public CallAgent(LlmService llmService) {
        super(llmService);
    }

    @Override
    public Object processInput(String input) {
        return input; // Pass raw input to LLM
    }

    @Override
    public Object decide(Object processedData) {
        String prompt = "User says: '" + processedData + "'. Provide troubleshooting steps for not being able to make phone calls.";
        return llmService.generateResponse(prompt);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean act(Object decision) {
        communicate((String) decision);
        return true;
    }

    @Override
    public void communicate(String message) {
        System.out.println("[CallAgent] " + message);
    }
}

